\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```","created_at":"2025-07-11T16:46:22Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T16:49:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#discussion_r2201270276","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108491","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201270276"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#discussion_r2201270276"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108491"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201270276/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":787,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2201227235,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":31,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201285550","pull_request_review_id":3011142928,"id":2201285550,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6DNPOu","diff_hunk":"@@ -790,43 +783,28 @@ void SceneTree::process_timers(double p_delta, bool p_physics_frame) {\n \t\ttimer->set_time_left(time_left);\n \n \t\tif (time_left <= 0) {\n-\t\t\tE->get()->emit_signal(SNAME(\"timeout\"));\n-\t\t\ttimers.erase(E);\n-\t\t}\n-\t\tif (E == L) {\n-\t\t\tbreak; // Break on last, so if new timers were added during list traversal, ignore them.\n+\t\t\ttimer->emit_signal(SNAME(\"timeout\"));\n+\t\t\ttimers.remove_at(i);","path":"scene/main/scene_tree.cpp","commit_id":"3b462f322834b09b5408a79f1f7606288da1014b","original_commit_id":"9dffe0ef04b1220e56b06447b6162497f831e03c","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Should work, but would need some evaluation because that's `O(n^2)` complexity, I don't think removing while processing is a good idea, I'd say the removal while working is exactly why `List` was picked, so this would need some benchmarking to evaluate the cost difference between:\r\n* One level of cache indirection\r\n* `O(n^2)` removal\r\n\r\n`O(n^2)` is because we move `n - i` elements each time we remove (all the elements after the current element), for the full vector we move `(n - 1) * (n - 2)` elements if my math's right","created_at":"2025-07-11T16:50:24Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T16:54:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#discussion_r2201285550","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108491","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201285550"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#discussion_r2201285550"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108491"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201285550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":787,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2201227235,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":31,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201358103","pull_request_review_id":3011252865,"id":2201358103,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6DNg8X","diff_hunk":"@@ -790,43 +783,28 @@ void SceneTree::process_timers(double p_delta, bool p_physics_frame) {\n \t\ttimer->set_time_left(time_left);\n \n \t\tif (time_left <= 0) {\n-\t\t\tE->get()->emit_signal(SNAME(\"timeout\"));\n-\t\t\ttimers.erase(E);\n-\t\t}\n-\t\tif (E == L) {\n-\t\t\tbreak; // Break on last, so if new timers were added during list traversal, ignore them.\n+\t\t\ttimer->emit_signal(SNAME(\"timeout\"));\n+\t\t\ttimers.remove_at(i);","path":"scene/main/scene_tree.cpp","commit_id":"3b462f322834b09b5408a79f1f7606288da1014b","original_commit_id":"9dffe0ef04b1220e56b06447b6162497f831e03c","user":{"login":"dementive","id":87823030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODIzMDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87823030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive","html_url":"https://github.com/dementive","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yeah I agree Im also not 100% sure this is still a gain with the slower removal.\r\n\r\nI suspect it still faster though because the List results in a cache miss on almost every iteration of timers/tweens and they are checked in both physics and regular processing. So with a 5 second timer that could be 600 cache misses with the List (probably a lot less you likely don't miss every time) at 60 FPS (I think that's how it works?) and for those 600 misses you only do 1 O(n^2) removal at the end of the timer.\r\n\r\nI could see situation where if there are thousands of 0.1 second timers/tweens this would end up being slower but the (likely?) more common case of having timers that last more than a few frames would end up being faster I think.\r\n\r\nWill write a benchmark to see what the difference is in cache misses and in timing for short and long timers/tweens to make sure all my assumptions aren't wrong though.","created_at":"2025-07-11T17:12:34Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T17:12:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#discussion_r2201358103","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108491","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201358103"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#discussion_r2201358103"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108491"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201358103/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":787,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2201227235,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":31,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2201366897","pull_request_review_id":3011266229,"id":2201366897,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOA